      "say": "In English, a bare Yes or No can sound cold. So we add a short answer: the pronoun plus the verb. Two rules. First, a yes answer never shortens: Yes, I am, never Yes, I'm. A no answer can: No, I'm not. Second, answer with a pronoun, not the name: Is Bat 12? Yes, he is.",
      "teach": "Stress falls on the last word of a yes short answer (Yes, I am), and a stressed word cannot be shortened. That is the real reason for the rule; the student only needs the rule itself. Say Yes, I am with clear stress on am.",
