      "say": "Line one: to say no, put not after the verb. Am not, isn't, aren't. And there is no amn't. [click] Line two: to ask, swap. The verb jumps to the front: Are you...? Where is...? Your voice goes up for yes or no questions, and down for question words. [click] Line three: answer with the pronoun and the verb. A yes stays full, Yes, I am. A no can be short, No, I'm not. Close: Now you can meet someone new in English, ask them where they are from and how old they are, and answer their questions naturally.",
